[1m[38;5;231mWhere should errors actually land?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mHosted service (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSentry or similar behind our own transport seam. Gets you alerting, dedup, and stack traces immediately; costs a [39m
     [38;5;246mvendor dependency and data egress.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Our own collect endpoint
     [38;5;246mPOST batched JSON to a receiver we build. No vendor, no egress — but there is no backend in this repo yet, so this
[39m     [38;5;246madds real server work beyond the logger.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Seam now, sink later
     [38;5;246mConsole transport today, real destination wired in a follow-up. Cheapest and reversible, but silent errors stay [39m
